<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech CSOB lowers key base rates by 25-50 bps.</title>
<headline>Czech CSOB lowers key base rates by 25-50 bps.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prague-based Ceskoslovenska Obchodni Banka (csob) said on Wednesday it cut its base lending rate for credit with a one- to two-year maturity 25 basis points to 14.75 percent.</p>
<p>In a statement, it said its base rate for two- to three-year credit was lowered 50 basis points to 14.25 percent. The moves follow a general down trend in rates on the Czech interbank markets.</p>
<p>-- John Mastrini, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
